{
  "stage": "verify",
  "item": "ch01.s08",
  "inputs_hash": "232625d2fe835b08caa2ab10d88226fc1f4e05117f4d0f531b5fe6f1f5e9cefa",
  "output_hash": "332446ff8077a58f75774c06a0bc34d46d46aed471dc13e5022d9dcbd9e87908",
  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch01.s08",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch01.s08.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.01",
            "text": "How can a model use earlier context when the words that matter may be far away from the current prediction?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.02",
            "text": "In this setting, attention is a technical term.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@217",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@219"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.03",
            "text": "A key part of the transformer architecture is the self-attention mechanism.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@237",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@238",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1256",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1261"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.04",
            "text": "Attention mechanisms have become an integral part of sequence modeling because they allow modeling dependencies without regard to distance in the input or output sequences.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1276",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1280",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1282",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1284",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1286"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.05",
            "text": "Put more concretely, attention lets the model relate different words even when those words are close together or far apart.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1293",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1295",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1297",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1299"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.06",
            "text": "Self-attention is an attention mechanism that relates different positions of a single sequence in order to compute a representation of that sequence.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1305",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1309",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1311",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1314",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1316"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p01.07",
            "text": "One useful intuition is that attention allows the model to weigh the importance of different words or tokens relative to each other.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1324",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1326",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1329",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1332",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1334"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch01.s08.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p02.r01",
            "text": "For example, suppose earlier sentences mention that Harry Potter is on a station or platform number something and that Harry Potter wants to board the train.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1334",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1337",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1340",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1342",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1344",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1346"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p02.r02",
            "text": "When predicting the next word in a fourth sentence, the context from sentences one, two, and three is important for understanding that fourth sentence and predicting its next word.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1348",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1350",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1353",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1355",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1358",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1360",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1362",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1365",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1367",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1368"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p02.r03",
            "text": "That is the meaning of long-range dependencies: when predicting the next word, the model needs to know the importance of previous words.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1370",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1373",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1376",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1377",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1380"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p02.r04",
            "text": "It needs to know how much attention to give to previous words and which earlier words should receive more attention, perhaps \"Harry,\" perhaps \"platform,\" or perhaps \"train.\"",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1380",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1382",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1385",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1387",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1388",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1391",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1393"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p02.r05",
            "text": "Self-attention captures these long-range dependencies so the model can look far behind, including sentences closer to the current one, to identify the next word.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1394",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1397",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1399",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1401",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1404",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1406"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch01.s08.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p03.01",
            "text": "The mechanism becomes easier to picture if you think in terms of scores over words.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p03.02",
            "text": "For next-word prediction, self-attention maintains an attention score that tells the model which word should receive more attention.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1418",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1421",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1423",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1425",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1428",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1429"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p03.03",
            "text": "That attention score is a matrix that tells the model which words should be given more importance in relation to other words.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1464",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1466",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1469",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1471",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1472",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1475"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p03.04",
            "text": "In the transformer architecture, attention appears in attention blocks such as multi-head attention and masked multi-head attention.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1441",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1443",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1445",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1447"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p03.05",
            "text": "These attention blocks help capture long-range dependencies in sentences, which is why the paper is called \"attention is all you need.\"",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1447",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1450",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1452",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1455",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1456",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1458"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch01.s08.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p04.01",
            "text": "There is also a helpful human analogy.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p04.02",
            "text": "People naturally keep context in mind while reading a story and remember what was written on the previous page.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1489",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1493",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1495",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1497",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1498"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p04.03",
            "text": "Self-attention gives a model a way to capture that long-range context, and this helps make next-word prediction accurate.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1501",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1504",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1506",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1508",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1511",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1513"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p04.04",
            "text": "In ChatGPT, the model gives attention to every sentence in the input when predicting the next word.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1513",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1516",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1519",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1521"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p04.05",
            "text": "It does not just look at the sentence immediately before the current one, because previous words may be more important.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1523",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1526",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1528",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1530",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1531",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@1533"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch01.s08.p04.06",
            "text": "Another way to think about self-attention is as parallel attention to different parts of a paragraph or to different sentences.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "NLn4eetGmf8@2259",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@2261",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@2263",
              "NLn4eetGmf8@2265"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
